RELEASE BINARIES ARE GPL-3.0
----------------------------

The prebuilt `vox` binaries attached to GitHub releases are built with the
`dist` feature set (cli, server, kokoro, piper). The `piper` feature links
espeak-ng statically, through the piper-rs and espeak-rs crates, to turn text
into phonemes. espeak-ng is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 or later.

A binary that contains espeak-ng is a combined work, so each release binary
is distributed, as a whole, under the GNU General Public License version 3
(LICENSE-GPL-3.0). The MIT and Apache-2.0 terms above continue to apply to
Vox's own source code; they are compatible with GPL-3.0, which is what allows
the combination.

The same holds for any binary you build yourself with the `piper`, `kokoro` or
`dist` feature: if you give that binary to someone else, you do so under GPL-3.0.

Corresponding source for a release binary is the repository at the release
tag (https://github.com/mrtozner/vox), including vendor/, together with the
crates.io dependencies at the exact versions pinned in Cargo.lock. espeak-ng's
source is part of the espeak-rs-sys crate.

OTHER BUILDS
------------

A build that enables `piper`, `dist` or `kokoro` contains espeak-ng or
material derived from it: the kokoro-tts crate compiles an English
phonemizer derived from espeak-ng's translator and embeds an espeak
dictionary. Treat such a binary as GPL-3.0 when you pass it on. Only a
build without those three features is free of espeak-ng material; its
license is determined by Vox's own MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms and by the
licenses of the dependencies of the features you enable. Review those
before redistributing your own build; `cargo tree --features <your
features>` lists them.

